# Normalize line endings: store text as LF, check out native.
* text=auto
*.go    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.marco text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
*.sum   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.ahk   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# The embedded web assets, which are READ BY TESTS and shipped inside a binary.
#
# `* text=auto` with core.autocrlf=true checks these out with CRLF, and Studio's page is
# asserted over byte by byte: `TestThePageBeginsAsADocument` reads the first line, and the
# page guards look for exact strings. A fresh clone therefore failed a test that passed for
# everyone who had never re-checked-out the file — found by walking this session's own
# commits to confirm each one builds.
#
# They are also go:embed'ed, so pinning LF keeps the asset byte-identical wherever it is
# built rather than varying with the checkout.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

# Batch files keep CRLF, which is what cmd.exe has always been given.
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Treat generated/binary artifacts as binary.
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.tar binary
*.zip binary

# Vision benchmark corpus images.
#
# Full-resolution 1920x1080 game frames: ~3MB each, and the corpus is expected to grow as
# sequences are added. Ordinary Git would keep every revision of every frame forever, and a
# benchmark corpus is exactly the wrong thing to store that way — the frames are replaced
# wholesale when a sequence is recaptured, never diffed.
#
# The MANIFEST and GROUND TRUTH stay in ordinary Git: they are small, they are edited by hand,
# and their history is the interesting one.
fixtures/vision/v2/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
